# Keeps the manager image build context small and reproducible: none of
# this is COPYed into deploy/docker/Dockerfile.manager, and excluding it
# here means a developer's local build artifacts, editor state or a large
# pre-existing web/node_modules tree can never accidentally change what
# gets built or leak into an image layer.
.git/
.github/
.idea/
.vscode/
.superpowers/
bin/
brand/
design/
docs/
web/node_modules/
web/dist/
web/coverage/
web/test-results/
web/playwright-report/
web/.tmp/
*.md
# Recursive: a slash-free pattern here is anchored to the context root and
# is NOT recursive, so ".env"/".env.*" alone would miss
# deploy/compose/.env — exactly the file the operator README tells people
# to create (cp .env.example .env) and that holds DB_PASSWORD and
# PULSIX_MASTER_KEY in plaintext. "**/" makes these match at any depth.
# The Dockerfile never reads .env.example, so it stays excluded too (it
# already matched "**/.env.*"); there is nothing in this build that needs
# any .env* file inside the image build context.
**/.env
**/.env.*
